<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="44d66897-d349-54f6-bc4a-383ebe1860e8" activityNameId="5fdf1f07-a48d-5f6f-abd0-761db23e9f72" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ventilation system, various components</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ventilation system, various components
Production of various components for a ventilation system with a nominal air flow rate of 5'000-20'000 m3/h at the air handling unit. Reference value of inventory is 1 m3/h nominal air flow of the air handling unit (at 2 m/s air speed in cross section of air filter or heat exchanger). The inventory is based on average data of 4 office buildings, 3 schools and 3 residential care homes with a total heated gross floor area of 61719 m2 and a total nominal air flow of 302190 m3/h, specific weight of the components: 0.17 kg/(m3/h), including average components for air valves, air intake, roof-hoods, dampers, fire dampers, silencers and sensors. The data represent a ventilation system mainly made of galvanized steel.
Materials used for the production. Energy use for the different production steps and for heating the production building. Transport of raw materials to the plant. Estimation for infrastructure of the production site included.
Location:  Data sources from different buildings in Switzerland. Process applicable in central European conditions.
Technology: Typical technology, materials and components used for ventilation systems in commercial and public buildings
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Process information partly from 2003 to 2012
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Data from different call of bids for ventilation system used. Data completed with information from literature and from manufacturers
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7f6f7ddd-1d8f-3843-9ffb-5790b51be31c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
